  "id": "COMPOUND:16022 - PROTEIN:987",
  "verbalization": "Dalbergichromene is implicated in the biological activity of Potassium voltage-gated channel subfamily D member 3 through a multi-step pathway. The drug targets Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta, which in turn is a target of 2-Hexulosonic acid and Maytansine, N(2')-deacetyl-N(2')-(3-methyl-1-oxobutyl)-. These compounds are known to interact with potassium voltage-gated channels, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Dalbergichromene may modulate these channels. The evidence supports a chain of interactions where Dalbergichromene indirectly influences the potassium voltage-gated channel subfamily D member 3 through its effects on diacylglycerol lipase and related compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Dalbergichromene in regulating potassium channel activity via a complex network of metabolic and signaling interactions.",
